From: ShizukuOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve standard-mode startup after combined DOS internals
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

Upstream: FDOS/kernel 5ffb5502d39a10a30f5b8a9e8beeba0bf30245d3 (ke2046)
Apply after 0003-cb43-win98-dos-internals.patch and
0003-dosmgr-honest-contract.patch. CB43 supplies the startup record layout,
prior veto, chain/self-link and actual-presence/version behavior. This final
patch preserves standard-mode registers/state instead of advertising an
unsupported enhanced-mode startup record. Do not insert a second optional
DWORD: the combined assembly already has the correct 22-byte startup header.
Protocol: Microsoft Windows 3.1 DDK Interrupt 2F/1605, DX bit0
https://dos-help.soulsphere.org/ddag31qh.hlp/Interrupt_2Fh_Function_1605h.html

--- a/kernel/inthndlr.c
+++ b/kernel/inthndlr.c
@@ -2041,7 +2041,7 @@
         /* RBIL 1605: honor an earlier veto and chain its startup record.
          * Do not turn a rejected startup into a reported Windows instance.
          */
-        if (r.CX)
+        if (r.CX || (r.DX & 1))
           break;
         if (r.es != FP_SEG(&winStartupInfo) || r.BX != FP_OFF(&winStartupInfo))
           winStartupInfo.next = ((ULONG)r.es << 16) | r.BX;
